    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` wasn't creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n**The Issue:**\nThe `gate` command in the frai CLI wasn't forwarding the `--ci` flag to the frai-gate CLI. This happened because the main `frai` program defines `.option('--ci', ...)`, which caused Commander.js to consume the flag at the main program level rather than passing it through to the subcommand.\n\n**The Fix:**\nModified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to:\n1. Update the `gate` command's action handler to receive the parent Command object\n2. Access the parent command's parsed options using `command.parent?.opts()`\n3. Check if `--ci` flag was set on the parent and add it to the arguments passed to the frai-gate CLI\n\n**Changes Made:**\n- Added `Command` type import from commander\n- Modified the gate command action handler to receive the `command` parameter\n- Reconstructed the arguments to include the `--ci` flag when present on the parent command\n- Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\n**Verification:**\nTesting confirmed that `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`",
